{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":769,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.32","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 32","reference":"Psalms 32","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The happiness of them whose sins are forgiven, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1, 2.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The necessity of confessing our sins, and of prayer, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"3-6.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"God's promise to them that trust in him, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"7-10.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"An exhortation to rejoice in God, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"A psalm of David, Maschil.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":10,"text":"Title of the psalm.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":11,"text":"Maschil - Or, an instructor.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":12,"text":"This psalm is fitly so called, because it was composed for the information of the church, in that most important doctrine, the way to true blessedness.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":13,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":14,"text":"Imputeth - Whom God doth not charge with the guilt of his sins, but graciously pardons and accepts him in Christ.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":15,"text":"No guile - Who freely confesses all his sins, and turns from sin to God with all his heart.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":16,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":17,"text":"Silence - From a full and open confession of my sins.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":18,"text":"Old - My spirit failed, and the strength of my body decayed.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":19,"text":"Roaring - Because of the continual horrors of my conscience, and sense of God's wrath.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":20,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":21,"text":"Hand - Thy afflicting hand.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":22,"text":"My moisture - Was dried up.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":23,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":24,"text":"The iniquity - The guilt of my sin.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":25,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":26,"text":"For this - Upon the encouragement of my example.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":27,"text":"Found - In an acceptable and seasonable time, while God continues to offer grace and mercy.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":28,"text":"Waters - In the time of great calamities.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":29,"text":"Not come - So as to overwhelm him.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":30,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":31,"text":"I will - This and the next verse seems to be the words of God, whom David brings in as returning this answer to his prayers.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":32,"text":"Mine eye - So Christ did St. Peter, when he turned and looked upon him.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":33,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":34,"text":"Will not - Unless they be forced to it by a bit or bridle.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":35,"text":"And so all the ancient translators understand it.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":36,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":37,"text":"Sorrows - This is an argument to enforce the foregoing admonition.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":32}}